  ; ⚠️ TWO WAYS ROUND DECODE (U2, docs/micro_ops_design.md). One machine,
  ; four instructions wide at fetch and eight behind it, four stages from
  ; fetch to dispatch -- and what it is with a cache of decoded micro-ops
  ; that delivers eight a cycle two stages out; with one no wider than
  ; decode, so that all it saves is the stages; with one that holds a single
  ; window, which a loop of two windows never finds anything in; and with a
  ; buffer that replays a loop of sixteen micro-ops without a break at its
  ; branch. All but the single window again on the engine that fetches what
  ; it predicts. Each cracks a load-and-add in two: the cache and the buffer
  ; count MICRO-OPS, and six instructions that are ten of those are two
  ; cycles of an eight-wide cache, not one.
